win32u: send WM_DPICHANGED on a cross-monitor move by default

Windows sends WM_DPICHANGED when a per-monitor-aware window moves to a monitor of another dpi. Our sender
(NEUTRON_DPI_34) was off since the 124 work, where it had destabilized Photoshop's floating windows. Without it,
Photoshop on a 100% screen next to a 175% one kept the 175% layout of its floating options bar at the bottom of
the screen (Contextual Task Bar 947x56 instead of 541x32).

On 138 with the sender on (lab copy of the operator's Photoshop 2026 on his Cintiq): the bar is normal size and his
drags between the two screens, floating and maximized, were clean. His call: on for every app, as on Windows.
Kill switch NEUTRON_DPI_34=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -2667,13 +2667,21 @@
 #define WM_DPICHANGED 0x02e0
 #endif
 
-/* NEUTRON: gate for the experimental cross-monitor WM_DPICHANGED sender (the ③+④ approach). OFF by
- * default — on Wayland the win32 window position is fictional so this fights the restore logic; the
- * shipping default relies on the winewayland driver-side scale fix. Set NEUTRON_DPI_34=1 to enable. */
+/* NEUTRON: gate for the cross-monitor WM_DPICHANGED sender (the ③+④ approach). ON by default since 2026-10-20:
+ * Windows sends WM_DPICHANGED when a per-monitor-aware window moves to a monitor of another dpi, and without it
+ * Photoshop on a 100% screen next to a 175% one kept the 175% layout of its floating options bar (Contextual Task
+ * Bar, 947x56 instead of 541x32). It was off since the 124 work, where it had destabilized Photoshop's floating
+ * windows; on 138 the operator's drags between the two screens, floating and maximized, were clean. Kill switch
+ * NEUTRON_DPI_34=0. */
 static BOOL neutron_dpi_34(void)
 {
     static int v = -1;
-    if (v < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_DPI_34" ); v = (e && e[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0; }
+    if (v < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_DPI_34" );
+        v = !e || e[0] != '0';
+        if (!v) ERR( "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DPI_34 = 0 (environment)\n" );
+    }
     return v;
 }
 
